   $q$Which part of the fable states the lesson most directly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The sentence about the summer rains coming","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-part"},{"text":"The last sentence, after the story ends","is_correct":true},{"text":"The sentence where Heron says thank you","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-part"},{"text":"The first sentence, about Beaver working all spring","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-part"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The last sentence, after the story ends$q$, $q$The last line, "A creek that is shared serves everyone well," stands on its own after the story and tells the lesson. Heron's thank you is part of the story's events, not the lesson itself.$q$, 'draft', '439aa76d-b98a-5180-bdd0-139c61b45fc8')
