-- Passage rg3-theme-summary-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a8f00fd1-6a23-50e7-8187-c78e4b01c4f3', 'rg3-theme-summary-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-theme-summary'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Two Basket Makers$q$, $q$Long ago, in a village beside a wide river, there lived two basket makers named Kofi and Ama.

One day the village chief made an announcement. "At the end of the week, I will choose one basket to carry rice at the harvest feast."

Kofi wanted to win quickly. Kofi grabbed the first reeds by the river, even the dry and cracked ones. By the end of the day, Kofi had made five baskets. "I am the fastest basket maker in the village!" Kofi called out.

Ama worked slowly. Ama soaked each reed in water until it bent without breaking. Ama pulled every row tight and checked it twice. By the end of the week, Ama had made only one basket.

At the feast, the chief filled one of Kofi's baskets with rice. As soon as it was lifted, the bottom split open. Rice spilled all over the ground.

Then the chief filled Ama's basket. It held every grain, and it did not bend at all.

The chief smiled. "Five weak baskets cannot carry what one strong basket can," the chief said.

The next week, Kofi went to Ama's house. "Will you show me how to soak the reeds?" Kofi asked. Ama nodded, and the two worked side by side.$q$, 'draft')
