insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('61b53cec-945d-576e-bc4d-4e3db67cf3c3', 'rg3-theme-summary-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-theme-summary'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Small Blue Square$q$, $q$The neighbors on Cedar Lane were painting a mural on the wall of the community center. Ms. Okafor, the art teacher, had drawn a giant picture of the town. There was a river, a bridge, a market, and a big orange sun.

Everyone got a part to paint. Lena painted the sun. Mr. Castillo painted the bridge. The twins, Hana and Jun, painted the market stalls.

Ravi got one small blue square in the corner. "That's it?" Ravi said. "Nobody will even notice this part."

Ravi painted the square fast and sloppy, then sat on the curb. When the mural was almost done, everyone stepped back to look.

"Something is wrong," Lena said. "The river looks like it stops in the middle of nowhere."

Ms. Okafor pointed to the corner. "The river is supposed to flow into this blue square. It's the lake. Without it, the river doesn't go anywhere."

Ravi looked at the messy square. Then Ravi picked up a brush. Slowly and carefully, Ravi painted small waves and a tiny boat. Ravi blended the blue of the lake into the blue of the river.

When Ravi stepped back, the whole mural looked different. The river now curved across the wall and ended in a shining lake.

"Now it looks finished," Mr. Castillo said.

Ravi grinned. The small blue square did not seem small anymore.$q$, 'draft')
