insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('28c593b8-74e2-5338-a6b1-2de8a4320ff1', 'rg3-word-parts-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Pancake Morning$q$, $q$On Sunday morning, Lena and Grandma Bea decided to make pancakes. Grandma Bea asked Lena to preheat the pan while they mixed the batter.

Lena read the recipe out loud. "Two cups of salt," Lena said. Grandma Bea laughed. "Look again. I think you misread it." Lena looked closer. The recipe said two cups of flour and just a pinch of salt!

Lena's little brother, Theo, wanted to help too. At first Theo was disagreeable. He wanted chocolate chips, and there were none. Then Grandma Bea found a bag of blueberries. Theo became much more agreeable and dropped the berries into the batter one by one.

The first pancake stuck to the pan. The second one was perfect, golden and fluffy. Lena flipped it high into the air and caught it.

When breakfast was ready, everyone sat down together. Theo said he was thankful for the blueberries. Lena was thankful for Grandma Bea's kindness and patience. It was the tastiest breakfast of the whole week.$q$, 'draft')
