   $q$What point does the author make in the second paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Knowing how to swim keeps children safer near water.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Families should only visit pools that have lifeguards.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Swimming lessons cost too much for many families.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaim"},{"text":"Swimming works the arms, the legs and the heart.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-paragraph"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Knowing how to swim keeps children safer near water.$q$, $q$The paragraph begins, "Swimming keeps children safe near water," and every sentence supports that. Working the arms and legs belongs to the next paragraph, about exercise.$q$, 'draft', 'dc3c8e03-86f7-55f4-88a7-c523f0066106')
