-- Passage rg4-comparing-texts-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b9c0e74d-9936-5576-8591-02f173126b21', 'rg4-comparing-texts-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Worth the Wait$q$, $q$Text 1: The Persimmon Tree (a story from Korea)

Every fall, Ji-woo watched the persimmon tree behind her grandmother's house. The fruit turned from green to orange. Ji-woo picked one early and took a big bite. It was so sour that her mouth felt dry and fuzzy.

Her grandmother laughed kindly. "The tree is not ready to share yet," she said. "Wait for the first frost."

Ji-woo waited. Each morning she checked the branches. At last, frost covered the yard. The persimmons were soft and dark orange. Ji-woo bit into one, and it tasted as sweet as honey.

Text 2: Maple Morning (a poem from Canada)

Grandpa says to wait,
so we wait.
The snow melts by day.
The nights stay cold.

Drip, drip, drip
into the metal pail.
It takes a whole bucket
to make one tiny jar.

We boil it all day long.
I want to taste it now!
Grandpa smiles and stirs.
"Good things take time."

At last, the golden syrup
pours over my pancakes.
I think Grandpa was right.
Waiting tastes sweet.$q$, 'draft')
