-- Passage rg4-comparing-texts-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('180a5a9d-3fc2-56a2-a577-f4cc99100880', 'rg4-comparing-texts-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Many Hands$q$, $q$Text 1: Moving the House (a story from the Philippines)

The Reyes family needed to move their small house closer to the road. The house was made of bamboo, and it stood on wooden posts. It was too heavy for one family to carry.

So the neighbors came. Twenty people slid long poles under the house. "One, two, three, lift!" called Mr. Reyes. Together they raised the whole house onto their shoulders. They walked slowly, step by step, across the field.

When the house was set down, Mrs. Reyes served rice cakes to everyone. The children ran in circles, cheering. Moving a house was hard work, but it felt like a party.

Text 2: Canal Day (a story from Peru)

High in the mountains, a small stream brought water to the village fields. Each spring, mud and rocks blocked the canal. One family alone could not clear it.

On canal day, every family brought shovels. Grandmothers carried baskets of potatoes and corn for lunch. Rosa, who was nine, picked up small stones and tossed them aside. By sunset, the water rushed freely down to the fields.

"Next year, it will be our turn to help again," Rosa's father said.$q$, 'draft')
